  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C046">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C046: Filtered_subset - has apo result for - Apo_coverage_statistic</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Apo_coverage_statistic"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/has_apo_result_for"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Filtered_subset"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>In Subset 2, 175,388 entries had at least one apo result. This corresponds to 39% of entries under those filtering criteria.</ahoj:claimText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C093">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C093: Unique_protein_ligand_interactions_499 - represent - Unique_ligands_193</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Unique_ligands_193"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/represent"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Unique_protein_ligand_interactions_499"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>The 499 unique protein-ligand interactions represent 193 unique ligands.</ahoj:claimText>
    <ahoj:sourceText>The search by UniProt AC provides an overview of known binding sites of the protein and a number of biologically relevant ligands found. It can be compared to the information provided by the PDBe-KB; if we look at glycogen phosphorylase from Oryctolagus cuniculus (UniProt AC: P00489 – see Figure 1) we can see 499 unique protein–ligand interactions – these represent 193 unique ligands, while PDBe-KB provides information about 198 known ligands – five of those are not biologically relevant according to BioLiP2 database. The result also shows us that the most common ligand is PLP that is forming 284 unique interactions in 130 structures. There are 16 sites corresponding to PLP-binding sites in APO form – it can be therefore used to study the variability of PLP binding and detect conformational changes between apo and holo structures. The results also show solvent accessible surface area calculated for the binding site (SASA), and the SASA normalized by the number of amino acids in the binding site that allows the analysis of the binding sites. More detailed information and visualizations of apo holo pairs are available through the 'View' or 'Download' buttons.</ahoj:sourceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Protein_structure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/Concept"/>
    <rdfs:label>Protein structure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label>Single holo representative structures</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label>Single protein structure</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label>Single rigid holo structures</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel>Single holo representative structures</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Single protein structure</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel>Single rigid holo structures</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:closeMatch rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/MacromolecularMachine"/>
    <skos:relatedMatch rdf:resource="https://www.rcsb.org/"/>
    <skos:scopeNote>Protein structures can be grounded by PDB identifiers.</skos:scopeNote>
    <skos:scopeNote>Protein structures can correspond to molecular assemblies; broad mapping.</skos:scopeNote>
    <ahoj:mappedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/External_KB_mapping_enrichment_2026_06_11"/>
    <ahoj:mergedEntityCount rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">3</ahoj:mergedEntityCount>
    <pred:rarely_captures rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Protein_conformational_variability"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C032">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C032: AHoJ_DB - reports - Structure_metrics</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Structure_metrics"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/reports"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/AHoJ_DB"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>AHoJ-DB reports metrics describing the whole candidate structure, including resolution and experimental method. These provide context for interpreting pocket-level comparisons.</ahoj:claimText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C057">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C057: Binding_pocket - can occur at - Interface_binding_pocket</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Interface_binding_pocket"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/can_occur_at"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Binding_pocket"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>The paper emphasizes that many protein-ligand binding sites are formed at interfaces between chains. These sites are important but harder to annotate across structures.</ahoj:claimText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/mappingPredicate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:label>mapping predicate</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
