    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>mapping set</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C071">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C071: AHoJ_DB - can support - Binding_site_analysis_use_case</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Binding_site_analysis_use_case"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/can_support"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/AHoJ_DB"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>The database records ligands, PTMs, and other factors that may occur on relevant chains or within pockets. These annotations can support studies of allosteric effects.</ahoj:claimText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C083">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C083: ent:Glycogen_phosphorylase_Oryctolagus_cuniculus - is concrete example for - ent:UniProt_search_use_case</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/UniProt_search_use_case"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/is_concrete_example_for"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Glycogen_phosphorylase_Oryctolagus_cuniculus"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>The AHoJ-DB paper uses glycogen phosphorylase from Oryctolagus cuniculus as a concrete example for search by UniProt accession.</ahoj:claimText>
    <ahoj:sourceText>The search by UniProt AC provides an overview of known binding sites of the protein and a number of biologically relevant ligands found. It can be compared to the information provided by the PDBe-KB; if we look at glycogen phosphorylase from Oryctolagus cuniculus (UniProt AC: P00489 – see Figure 1) we can see 499 unique protein–ligand interactions – these represent 193 unique ligands, while PDBe-KB provides information about 198 known ligands – five of those are not biologically relevant according to BioLiP2 database. The result also shows us that the most common ligand is PLP that is forming 284 unique interactions in 130 structures. There are 16 sites corresponding to PLP-binding sites in APO form – it can be therefore used to study the variability of PLP binding and detect conformational changes between apo and holo structures. The results also show solvent accessible surface area calculated for the binding site (SASA), and the SASA normalized by the number of amino acids in the binding site that allows the analysis of the binding sites. More detailed information and visualizations of apo holo pairs are available through the 'View' or 'Download' buttons.</ahoj:sourceText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C019">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C019: Candidate_structures - are restricted to - UniProt_accession</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/UniProt_accession"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/are_restricted_to"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Candidate_structures"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>AHoJ-DB searches for candidate pockets only in structures assigned to the same UniProt accession as the query protein. This constrains comparisons to structures of the same protein sequence context.</ahoj:claimText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/claim/C029">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ClaimTriplet"/>
    <rdfs:label>C029: Candidate_structures - use maximum resolution - Distance_cutoff_4_5_angstrom</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Article_AHoJDB_2024"/>
    <ahoj:claimObject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Distance_cutoff_4_5_angstrom"/>
    <ahoj:claimPredicate rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/predicate/use_maximum_resolution"/>
    <ahoj:claimSubject rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Candidate_structures"/>
    <ahoj:claimText>For filtered results displayed in AHoJ-DB, the authors used a softer post-processing filter with a 4.5 Å resolution threshold. These filtered results are separate from the broader processed results.</ahoj:claimText>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/claimObject">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property"/>
    <rdfs:label>claim object</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/Metric">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Structural or dataset metric</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ResearchProblem">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Research problem or motivation</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/Mapping_Bio2RDF_Bio2RDF">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/ontology/ExternalMapping"/>
    <rdfs:label>Bio2RDF mapping to Bio2RDF</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasGeneratedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/ahoj/entity/External_KB_mapping_enrichment_2026_06_11"/>
    <ahoj:mappingObject rdf:resource="https://bio2rdf.org/"/>
